{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>A man, a man.</b> Every man. And since he did not mention 'of the house of Israel,' we do not abandon the stranger [i.e., the ger] so that he may commit any of the abominations mentioned in our land and not defile the land." "<b>To any close flesh.</b> A general term for all the forbidden unions, and afterward he specifies. And Rabbi Aaron the Priest said its meaning is to exclude emission of seed for nothing." "<b>You shall not approach.</b> A euphemism for lying with. And likewise ואקרב אל הנביאה (and I drew near to the prophetess). And קרוב (approach) is close to the word מאל תגשו אל אשה (from 'do not approach a woman')." "<b>Ervah.</b> A shameful thing, exposed, needing to be covered." "And the meaning of <b>I am HaShem.</b> is that HaShem loves separation for His servant and to hear His word, and Mount Sinai is a witness, also the first one [commandment], and it is the sod of man. And because the inclination of man's heart is like beasts, it is impossible to forbid all females, so He forbade all those found with him at all times. And in the parashah Ki Tetze, camp, I shall reveal to you a sod sealed and closed. And behold, all who make themselves impure distance themselves from the name HaShem, the received one; therefore he mentioned 'I am HaShem.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {4 "The phrase 'ובפרשה כי תצא מחנה' is textually difficult: מחנה (camp) does not fit syntactically after Ki Tetze. Translated hyper-literally as printed. The reading may be corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:44.785949831Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}